1
00:00:01,970 --> 00:00:05,550
There's a conversation we have to finish.

2
00:00:05,550 --> 00:00:08,100
What was it about?

3
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:09,920
It was about caring.

4
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:12,620
Oh?

5
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:14,900
Yes, caring.

6
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:16,760
I said that it makes me feel good

7
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:18,930
that you care about Michelle.

8
00:00:18,930 --> 00:00:20,990
Well, I do care about Michelle.

9
00:00:20,990 --> 00:00:24,930
And it makes me feel good that you care about me.

10
00:00:24,930 --> 00:00:26,920
You know I do.

11
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:32,640
You're a ... wonderful friend.

12
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:34,120
And it makes me feel good

13
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:38,450
that you care about us.

14
00:00:38,450 --> 00:00:41,120
Well ... well,

15
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:42,140
I do, Harry.

16
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:45,460
It's only natural that if I care about Michelle

17
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:48,060
and I care about you,

18
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:50,720
then I care about us.

19
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:51,790
It's OK, Susan.

20
00:00:51,790 --> 00:00:53,100
We had this part of the conversation

21
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:54,160
before Michelle and her friends arrived.

22
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:57,510
Now comes the good part.

23
00:00:57,510 --> 00:00:58,580
Like what?

24
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:01,790
Well, assume that if you care about Michelle

25
00:01:01,790 --> 00:01:02,950
and you care about me

26
00:01:02,950 --> 00:01:05,510
and you care about us,

27
00:01:05,510 --> 00:01:07,960
that we can talk about us.

28
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:11,720
I mean--you and me.

29
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:14,880
Isn't that right?

30
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:20,590
What are you trying to say, Harry?

31
00:01:20,590 --> 00:01:24,460
What I'm trying to say ...

32
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:29,830
since this is so easy ....

33
00:01:29,830 --> 00:01:54,210
Here are ten letters that express my feelings for you.

34
00:01:54,210 --> 00:01:56,430
Don't be silly, Harry.

35
00:01:56,430 --> 00:01:57,670
You want a hint?

36
00:01:57,670 --> 00:01:58,970
It's two words.

37
00:01:58,970 --> 00:02:02,340
You're making the game harder.

38
00:02:02,340 --> 00:02:04,300
Can't you figure it out?

39
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:06,190
Seven letters ... two words ...

40
00:02:06,190 --> 00:02:09,680
that express the feelings that I feel for you in my heart.

41
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:29,960
Harry, I get it! Harry

42
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:33,630
Well? Does that mean you'll marry me?

43
00:02:33,630 --> 00:02:43,000
Is that a proposal, or are we just playing a game?

44
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:48,310
Sit down, Susan.

45
00:02:48,310 --> 00:03:05,100
There's something I have to ask you.

46
00:03:05,100 --> 00:03:09,920
Susan, will you marry me?

47
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:12,100
It's such an important decision.

48
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:15,250
There's so many things to talk about.

49
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:19,110
There are three things that have to be done first, Harry.

50
00:03:19,110 --> 00:03:20,630
Three things?

51
00:03:20,630 --> 00:03:24,100
First, we have to decide where to live.

52
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:25,250
Well, that's easy.

53
00:03:25,250 --> 00:03:26,330
We talked about that earlier.

54
00:03:26,330 --> 00:03:27,260
We'll live in New York.

55
00:03:27,260 --> 00:03:29,370
All right.

56
00:03:29,370 --> 00:03:30,210
Second,

57
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:34,070
we have to talk to Michelle together about being married.

58
00:03:34,070 --> 00:03:36,310
We'll do that immediately.

59
00:03:36,310 --> 00:03:38,270
What's the third thing?

60
00:03:38,270 --> 00:03:40,520
You have to ask for my father's permission.

61
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:42,700
Absolutely!

62
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:44,060
But first things first.

63
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:47,450
We have to go pick up Michelle.

64
00:03:47,450 --> 00:03:52,030
Oh, I'm so happy, Harry!

65
00:03:52,030 --> 00:03:55,030
Not as happy as I am.
